Mitcad patch (mitcad#343): a contact that ends on the spine's own edge near
the vertex where the spine goes on passes that vertex.

The rounding round a thread's chamfer cone (radius 0.5) runs, as one
contour, along the cone's edges with an earlier rounding of the crest and
then with the thread's flank, which goes on tangentially from it across an
edge ending at the vertex V between the two edges of the contour. The cone
and the earlier rounding meet at 1.7 degrees at V, so the blend there is
0.015 wide, its contacts 7.5 micrometres from the edge; the stored edges lie
up to 4 micrometres off their faces. The walk's contact on the earlier
rounding met the edge with the cone itself, 0.034 before V (the vertex's
tolerance 0.0042), and the walk ended there: a ball cannot touch its face
across its own edge with the blend's other face, and SearchFace found the
cone beyond, not a face continuing that one. ChFi3d_OwnEdgeNearVertex takes
such a contact point (on the edge of the spine between the contact's face
and the blend's other face, within ten times its tolerance or its vertex's
of the vertex ahead, where the spine goes on into another of its edges and
a face tangent to the contact's face holds that edge) at that vertex, with
the contact's way as its vector: SearchFace and StartSol go on through the
vertex into that face (SearchFaceOnV), and the walk goes on along the
spine's next edge.

